# Flying with a flight controller (ANGLE, ACRO). The plain T1-S has none; a plane that does,
# like the T1-S VTOL, can. The sim's own stick modes are built (src/sim.rs). The tests that need
# a flight controller run with ArduPilot beside the sim: `--aircraft t1s-vtol --direct --expect`. See also the
# ground station, which flies the VTOL with ArduPilot and a radio.

Section: Flying with a flight controller
  A plane with a flight controller can help the pilot. The T1-S VTOL has one, and the T1-S
  Ranger, which is a plain plane, does not. With a flight controller the sim has three flight modes: MANUAL, [[ANGLE]] and [[ACRO]].
  On a keyboard, M selects the next one. On a radio, the switch you gave to ArduPilot mode
  does it.

  The T1-S VTOL flies with ArduPilot too, and the six buttons on the front of the radio are its
  flight modes: [[QHOVER]], [[QLOITER]], [[FBWA]], [[CRUISE]], [[AUTO]] and [[QRTL]]. [[The six buttons of the radio]]
  says what each one does. [[Flying a VTOL with self-levelling]] is a tutorial that uses them.

  The DeepSpace Seeker 3 is a quadcopter, so it has no wing and no forward-flight modes. ArduPilot flies it
  as a quadplane with a quad frame, and its radio has six modes: QHOVER, QLOITER, GUIDED, AUTO, QRTL and
  QLAND. The hover tests of this section run on both planes.

Vocabulary:
  Phrase: the sim has just started with a flight controller
    Say: start the sim with the T1-S VTOL. In [[The launcher]], click SIMULATOR ONLY, then WITH ARDUPILOT, then LAUNCH. (From source, you can instead run `cargo run --release --bin sim001`.) To fly the Seeker 3 quadcopter, click SEEKER 3 (LIGHT QUAD) first, or add `-- --aircraft seeker3`. The sim opens at the pilot box with a plane that has a flight controller. The plane is on the ground, the throttle is closed and the flight mode is MANUAL
    Given the flight controller is fitted
    And the throttle is 0 %
    And the pitch stick is centred
    And the roll stick is centred
    And the flight mode is MANUAL
    And the sim is running

  Event: the pilot arms the plane
    Say: press B, the arm switch of ArduPilot
  Event: the pilot opens the throttle to climb
    Say: press 4. In the hover modes, the throttle sets how fast the plane climbs. On the keyboard, each throttle above 0 % is a climb
  Event: the pilot sends the plane home
    Say: switch ArduPilot to QRTL. On the radio, press button 6 on the front. On the keyboard, press N until the mode is QRTL. The plane flies to home, and lands there
  State: the autopilot is armed | disarmed
    Shows: armed: the line at the top of the HUD says ARMED
    Shows: disarmed: the line at the top of the HUD says disarmed

Background:
  Given the sim has just started with a flight controller
